.TH RPSHOW 1 2026-11-09 "rpshow 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rpshow \- show a local file in a fullscreen pager on a Raspberry Pi screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rpshow
.RI [ OPTION ]...\& " FILE"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpshow
copies the local
.I FILE
over
.BR ssh (1)
to a temporary directory on a remote host and shows it there in
.BR less (1),
inside a new fullscreen
.B alacritty
window on the host's X display.
It is meant for a Raspberry Pi with a monitor and a mouse but no keyboard.
The mouse wheel scrolls.
A right click closes the window; the pager and the remote copy of
.I FILE
go with it.
Quitting
.B less
closes the window too.
.PP
The remote copy keeps the base name of
.IR FILE ,
so
.B lesspipe
on the remote host can pick a filter by its extension.
.SS Markdown
A
.I FILE
whose name ends in
.BR .md ,
.BR .markdown ,
.BR .mdown ,
.BR .mkd ,
.B .mkdn
or
.B .mdwn
(in any case) is rendered before it is shown:
headings, emphasis, lists, tables, quotes, links and code blocks are
laid out and coloured to fit the window, and
.B less
shows the result.
The rendering is done on the remote host by the
.B rich
Python module, as
.PP
.EX
python3 \-m rich.markdown \-c \fIFILE\fP | less \-R
.EE
.PP
run inside the window, so the text is wrapped to the window's width.
This is what
.B python3 \-m rich.markdown \-c \-p
.I FILE
does in a local terminal.
.B \-R
is added to the
.B less
options so the colours show, and
.B PYTHONIOENCODING=utf\-8
is set so the box and bullet characters survive a remote locale that
is not UTF\-8.
Older
.B rich
releases render less: version 9.11 (Raspberry Pi OS 11) shows tables
as their source text.
.PP
If the remote
.B python3
cannot import
.BR rich ,
.B rpshow
says so on standard error and shows the Markdown source instead.
On Raspberry Pi OS and Debian the module is in the
.B python3\-rich
package.
Use
.B \-\^\-raw
to show the source on purpose.
.SS PDF
A
.I FILE
whose name ends in
.B .pdf
(in any case), or whose first bytes are
.BR %PDF\- ,
is shown in
.BR zathura (1)
instead of
.BR less ,
fullscreen and without status or input bar.
The mouse wheel scrolls and a right click closes the window, as with
other files.
A PDF found by its first bytes alone gets
.B .pdf
appended to its remote name.
.PP
The pages are recoloured dark, the way
.B zathura
does with
.BR "set recolor true" .
The colours come from the local
.BR zathurarc :
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zathura/zathurarc
or else
.BR ~/.config/zathura/zathurarc .
Only
.B set
lines for these options are passed on:
.BR adjust\-open ,
.BR default\-bg ,
.BR default\-fg ,
.BR recolor ,
.BR recolor\-darkcolor ,
.BR recolor\-keephue ,
.BR recolor\-lightcolor ,
.BR recolor\-reverse\-video ,
.BR render\-loading ,
.B render\-loading\-bg
and
.BR render\-loading\-fg ,
and only with a value made of letters, digits, spaces and
.BR #(),.%+\- ,
such as
.B rgba(0,0,0,1)
or a quoted
.BR \(dq#000000\(dq .
Other lines, mappings and
.B include
are ignored.
So a
.B set recolor false
in the local file turns the recolouring off, and without a local
.B zathurarc
the PDF is recoloured with
.BR zathura 's
default colours.
.B \-\^\-light
shows the pages in their own colours.
.PP
.B zathura
gets a configuration, data and cache directory of its own next to the
remote copy, so the remote host's
.B zathurarc
is not read and no history of the PDF is kept there.
If the remote host has no
.BR zathura ,
.B rpshow
says so on standard error and shows the PDF as text in
.BR less ,
the way
.B \-\^\-raw
does: through
.B lesspipe
and
.BR pdftotext ,
when the remote host has them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-H " HOST" "\fR, \fP\-\^\-host=" HOST
Connect to
.IR HOST ,
any destination
.BR ssh (1)
accepts.
The default is
.B $RPSHOW_HOST
or else
.BR pi .
.TP
.BI \-d " DISPLAY" "\fR, \fP\-\^\-display=" DISPLAY
Open the window on X display
.I DISPLAY
of the remote host.
The default is
.BR :0 .
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\^\-wait
Wait until the window is closed, and exit with the terminal's status.
Without this option
.B rpshow
returns about a second after the window opened, or with the terminal's
error output and status if it failed to start.
.IP
Either way, if
.B alacritty
reports within that second that it ignored one of its settings or found
an error in its configuration,
.B rpshow
closes the window, prints the terminal's messages and exits with status 1:
such a window might be neither fullscreen nor closable with a right click.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\^\-raw
Show a Markdown
.I FILE
as it is, like any other file, instead of rendering it (see
.BR Markdown ),
and a PDF
.I FILE
as text in
.B less
instead of in
.B zathura
(see
.BR PDF ).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\^\-light
Show a PDF
.I FILE
in its own colours, without the dark recolouring (see
.BR PDF ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\^\-verbose
Report the
.B less
options that were dropped (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ),
and the warnings
.B zathura
printed within a second of starting, such as an option the remote
.B zathura
does not know.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\^\-help
Display a usage message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\^\-version
Display version information and exit.
.PP
When
.B POSIXLY_CORRECT
is set, options must come before
.IR FILE .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RPSHOW_LESS
Options for the remote
.BR less ,
passed to it as its
.B LESS
variable.
If unset or empty,
.B LESS
is used, so the remote pager behaves like the local one; if that is
empty too,
.BR \-R .
Options the remote
.B less
rejects are dropped, since a keyboardless screen cannot dismiss the
error prompt, and so is
.BR \-\^\-mouse ,
which would keep the right click from reaching the terminal.
The remote side also sets
.BR LESSCHARSET=utf-8 ,
.B LESSSECURE=1
and
.BR LESSSECURE_ALLOW=lessopen ,
so
.B lesspipe
still works in secure mode with a
.B less
that knows
.B LESSSECURE_ALLOW
(less 710 does; less 551, in Raspberry Pi OS 11, does not).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the local
.B zathurarc
is looked for (see
.BR PDF ),
if set to an absolute path; otherwise
.BR ~/.config .
.TP
.B RPSHOW_HOST
Default destination for
.BR \-H .
.TP
.B RPSHOW_SSH
The
.BR ssh (1)
program to run, found in
.B PATH
if it contains no slash.
The default is
.BR ssh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 for usage errors, unreadable files (including an
unreadable local
.BR zathurarc )
and a terminal that rejected its settings, 126 or 127 if
the ssh program cannot be run, otherwise the exit status of
.BR ssh (1),
which reports that of the remote terminal or
.BR zathura .
.SH NOTES
The window settings are given to
.B alacritty
as TOML overrides with
.BR \-o ,
such as
.BR mouse.bindings ,
so
.B alacritty
0.13 or later is required.
.PP
Markdown rendering needs
.B python3
with the
.B rich
module on the remote host.
.PP
Showing PDFs needs
.B zathura
0.4.7 or later, with its PDF plugin
.RB ( zathura\-pdf\-poppler
on Raspberry Pi OS and Debian), on the remote host.
.B alacritty
is not needed for them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
rpshow notes.txt
rpshow \-w \-H otherpi \-d :1 report.md
rpshow \-\^\-raw README.md
rpshow paper.pdf
rpshow \-\^\-light scan.pdf
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR alacritty (1),
.BR zathura (1),
.BR zathurarc (5)
